IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgn-register`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), Part 11A, LAYER 1, fifth module: ss 386AKA (the register of nominee directors), 386AL (nominee directors), 386ALA (the register
-- of nominee shareholders) and 386ALB (nominee shareholders).
--
-- THE TIME LIMITS. Each paragraph that gives a time gives it in days: "within 30 days after", "within 60 days after", "within 7 days after", or none ("on that date",
-- which is the day itself, 0 days). The counting is `period: the last day of a period after` (sg-periods.l4) and the helper `s 386AF(8) timing: the act was done in time`
-- (sgn-register.l4): JUST TRUE (done on or before the last day), JUST FALSE (done late, or not done and the last day has passed), NOTHING (not done, and the last day has not passed).
--
-- THE APPOINTED DAY. s 386AL(9) and s 386ALB(8) each define "appointed day" as the commencement of a section of the 2024 Act (section 8 and section 10: different sections, so
-- two inputs; the same date in fact, assumed; fork F-AL1). The 2024 Act is not a source, so each date is an input.
--
-- THE PRESCRIBED THINGS (the particulars, the form and the place of a register) are inputs named for the fact.
--
-- READING A RESULT: see the header of sgn-application.l4.

§ `Section 386AKA: the register of nominee directors`

-- (1): keep the register. Fork F-AKA1: "registered under Division 2 of Part 11" is read as qualifying "foreign company" (a company is incorporated, not registered under Division 2 of Part 11);
-- the other reading makes it qualify both, which would leave a company that is not registered under that Division outside the duty. The scope is therefore ONE input, true for a company
-- and for a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11.
-- src:26343 | 386AKA.—(1) A company or foreign company registered under
-- src:26344 | Division 2 of Part 11 must keep a register of its directors who are
-- src:26345 | nominees (called in this Part the register of nominee directors) in the
-- src:26346 | prescribed form and at the prescribed place.
@ref s 386AKA(1) (src:26343-26346)
GIVEN `the body is a company, or a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body has kept a register of its directors who are nominees in the prescribed form and at the prescribed place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AKA(1) the company or foreign company has kept the register of nominee directors as required` MEANS
    IF NOT `the body is a company, or a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1) speaks of "A company or foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11"
    ELSE (IF `the body has kept a register of its directors who are nominees in the prescribed form and at the prescribed place`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question): "must keep a register of its directors who are nominees ... in the prescribed form and at the prescribed place"; no time is fixed, so a register not kept on the date asked is the failure (as for s 386AF(7))

-- src:26348 | (2) Subject to section 386AM, a company or foreign company must
-- src:26349 | not disclose, or make available for inspection, the register of nominee
-- src:26350 | directors or any particulars contained in the register of nominee
-- src:26351 | directors to any member of the public.
@ref s 386AKA(2) (src:26348-26351)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386AKA act`
`s 386AKA(2) a company or foreign company must not disclose the register of nominee directors to a member of the public` MEANS
    PARTY `the company or foreign company`
    SHANT `s 386AKA(2) disclose the register of nominee directors or any particulars in it, or make it available for inspection, to a member of the public`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the company or foreign company` BECAUSE "the company disclosed the register of nominee directors or its particulars, or made it available for inspection, to a member of the public (s 386AKA(2), (6))"

-- src:26343 | 386AKA.—(1) A company or foreign company registered under
-- src:26344 | Division 2 of Part 11 must keep a register of its directors who are
-- src:26345 | nominees (called in this Part the register of nominee directors) in the
-- src:26346 | prescribed form and at the prescribed place.
@ref s 386AKA(1) (src:26343-26346)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386AKA act`
`s 386AKA(1) a company or foreign company must keep a register of nominee directors` MEANS
    PARTY `the company or foreign company`
    MUST `s 386AKA(1) keep a register of its directors who are nominees in the prescribed form and at the prescribed place`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 386AKA(1) gives this duty no deadline in days (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- (2): the bar. "Subject to section 386AM": a disclosure under that section lifts it.
-- src:26348 | (2) Subject to section 386AM, a company or foreign company must
-- src:26349 | not disclose, or make available for inspection, the register of nominee
-- src:26350 | directors or any particulars contained in the register of nominee
-- src:26351 | directors to any member of the public.
@ref s 386AKA(2) (src:26348-26351)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made in compliance with a requirement made, or in the exercise of a power conferred, under section 386AM` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AKA(2) the company or foreign company is barred from disclosing the register of nominee directors to the person` MEANS
    IF `the disclosure is made in compliance with a requirement made, or in the exercise of a power conferred, under section 386AM`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to section 386AM, a company or foreign company must not disclose ..." read as: where the disclosure is under s 386AM the bar does not apply
    ELSE (IF `the person is a member of the public`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on disclosure "to any member of the public" (s 386AB defines the term); a person who is not one is outside the limit

-- (3), (4), (5): enter within 7 days after the company is informed.
-- src:26353 | (3) A company or foreign company must, within 7 days after the
-- src:26354 | company or foreign company is informed of any fact and provided
-- src:26355 | with any particulars mentioned in section 386AL(1), (1A), (2), (4) or
-- src:26356 | (5), enter that fact and those particulars in its register of nominee
-- src:26357 | directors.
@ref s 386AKA(3) (src:26353-26357)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company has entered the fact and the particulars in its register of nominee directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company or foreign company entered the fact and the particulars` IS A DATE
      `the day the company or foreign company was informed of the fact and provided with the particulars` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AKA(3) the company or foreign company has entered the fact and the particulars in time` MEANS
    `s 386AF(8) timing: the act was done in time` `the company or foreign company has entered the fact and the particulars in its register of nominee directors` `the day the company or foreign company entered the fact and the particulars` `the day the company or foreign company was informed of the fact and provided with the particulars` 7 `the date asked`   -- FALSE-kind where late ("within 7 days after the company or foreign company is informed": a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a)); NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) while the 7 days have not run out

-- src:26353 | (3) A company or foreign company must, within 7 days after the
-- src:26354 | company or foreign company is informed of any fact and provided
-- src:26355 | with any particulars mentioned in section 386AL(1), (1A), (2), (4) or
-- src:26356 | (5), enter that fact and those particulars in its register of nominee
-- src:26357 | directors.
@ref s 386AKA(3) (src:26353-26357)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386AKA act`
`s 386AKA(3) a company or foreign company must enter the fact and the particulars in its register of nominee directors within 7 days after it is informed` MEANS
    PARTY `the company or foreign company`
    MUST `s 386AKA(3) enter the fact and the particulars in its register of nominee directors`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the company or foreign company` BECAUSE "the company did not enter the fact and the particulars in its register of nominee directors within 7 days after it was informed (s 386AKA(3), (6))"

-- src:26359 | (4) A company or foreign company must, within 7 days after the
-- src:26360 | company or foreign company is informed under section 386AL(3)(a)
-- src:26361 | or (5A)(a) that a director of the company or foreign company has
-- src:26366 | ceased to be a nominee, enter the following in the company’s or
-- src:26367 | foreign company’s register of nominee directors:
-- src:26369 | (a) the fact that the director has ceased to be a nominee;
-- src:26371 | (b) the date on which the director ceased to be a nominee.
@ref s 386AKA(4) (src:26359-26371)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company has entered the fact that the director has ceased to be a nominee and the date on which the director ceased to be a nominee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company or foreign company entered them` IS A DATE
      `the day the company or foreign company was informed that a director has ceased to be a nominee` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AKA(4) the company or foreign company has entered the cessation in time` MEANS
    `s 386AF(8) timing: the act was done in time` `the company or foreign company has entered the fact that the director has ceased to be a nominee and the date on which the director ceased to be a nominee` `the day the company or foreign company entered them` `the day the company or foreign company was informed that a director has ceased to be a nominee` 7 `the date asked`   -- FALSE-kind where late ("within 7 days after the company or foreign company is informed ... that a director ... has ceased to be a nominee": ruling (a)); NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) while the 7 days have not run out

-- src:26359 | (4) A company or foreign company must, within 7 days after the
-- src:26360 | company or foreign company is informed under section 386AL(3)(a)
-- src:26361 | or (5A)(a) that a director of the company or foreign company has
-- src:26366 | ceased to be a nominee, enter the following in the company’s or
-- src:26367 | foreign company’s register of nominee directors:
-- src:26369 | (a) the fact that the director has ceased to be a nominee;
-- src:26371 | (b) the date on which the director ceased to be a nominee.
@ref s 386AKA(4) (src:26359-26371)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386AKA act`
`s 386AKA(4) a company or foreign company must enter the cessation of a director as a nominee within 7 days after it is informed` MEANS
    PARTY `the company or foreign company`
    MUST `s 386AKA(4) enter the fact that the director has ceased to be a nominee and the date on which the director ceased to be a nominee`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the company or foreign company` BECAUSE "the company did not enter the cessation of the director as a nominee within 7 days after it was informed (s 386AKA(4), (6))"

-- src:26373 | (5) A company or foreign company must, within 7 days after the
-- src:26374 | company or foreign company is informed under section 386AL(3)(b)
-- src:26375 | or (5A)(b) of any change to the particulars of a person for whom a
-- src:26376 | director of the company or foreign company is a nominee, enter the
-- src:26377 | following in the company’s or foreign company’s register of nominee
-- src:26378 | directors:
-- src:26380 | (a) the new particulars of that person;
-- src:26382 | (b) the date on which the particulars of that person changed.
@ref s 386AKA(5) (src:26373-26382)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company has entered the new particulars of the person for whom a director is a nominee and the date on which they changed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the company or foreign company entered them` IS A DATE
      `the day the company or foreign company was informed of the change to the particulars` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AKA(5) the company or foreign company has entered the change in time` MEANS
    `s 386AF(8) timing: the act was done in time` `the company or foreign company has entered the new particulars of the person for whom a director is a nominee and the date on which they changed` `the day the company or foreign company entered them` `the day the company or foreign company was informed of the change to the particulars` 7 `the date asked`   -- FALSE-kind where late ("within 7 days after the company or foreign company is informed ... of any change to the particulars": ruling (a)); NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) while the 7 days have not run out

-- src:26373 | (5) A company or foreign company must, within 7 days after the
-- src:26374 | company or foreign company is informed under section 386AL(3)(b)
-- src:26375 | or (5A)(b) of any change to the particulars of a person for whom a
-- src:26376 | director of the company or foreign company is a nominee, enter the
-- src:26377 | following in the company’s or foreign company’s register of nominee
-- src:26378 | directors:
-- src:26380 | (a) the new particulars of that person;
-- src:26382 | (b) the date on which the particulars of that person changed.
@ref s 386AKA(5) (src:26373-26382)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386AKA act`
`s 386AKA(5) a company or foreign company must enter the new particulars within 7 days after it is informed of a change` MEANS
    PARTY `the company or foreign company`
    MUST `s 386AKA(5) enter the new particulars of the person for whom a director is a nominee and the date on which they changed`
    WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the company or foreign company` BECAUSE "the company did not enter the new particulars within 7 days after it was informed of the change (s 386AKA(5), (6))"

DECLARE `s 386AKA act` IS ONE OF
    `s 386AKA(2) disclose the register of nominee directors or any particulars in it, or make it available for inspection, to a member of the public`
    `s 386AKA(1) keep a register of its directors who are nominees in the prescribed form and at the prescribed place`
    `s 386AKA(3) enter the fact and the particulars in its register of nominee directors`
    `s 386AKA(4) enter the fact that the director has ceased to be a nominee and the date on which the director ceased to be a nominee`
    `s 386AKA(5) enter the new particulars of the person for whom a director is a nominee and the date on which they changed`

-- (6): the offence of the company and every officer in default.
-- src:26384 | (6) If a company or foreign company fails to comply with
-- src:26385 | subsection (1), (2), (3), (4) or (5), the company or foreign
-- src:26386 | company, and every officer of the company or foreign company
-- src:26387 | who is in default, shall each be guilty of an offence and shall each be
-- src:26388 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $25,000.
@ref s 386AKA(6) (src:26384-26388)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company fails to comply with subsection (1), (2), (3), (4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AKA(6) the company or foreign company is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the company or foreign company fails to comply with subsection (1), (2), (3), (4) or (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question; split site (i)): "shall each be guilty of an offence and shall each be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $25,000"

-- src:26384 | (6) If a company or foreign company fails to comply with
-- src:26385 | subsection (1), (2), (3), (4) or (5), the company or foreign
-- src:26386 | company, and every officer of the company or foreign company
-- src:26387 | who is in default, shall each be guilty of an offence and shall each be
-- src:26388 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $25,000.
@ref s 386AKA(6) (src:26384-26388)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company fails to comply with subsection (1), (2), (3), (4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, as section 408(3) gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AKA(6) the officer of the company or foreign company is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the company or foreign company fails to comply with subsection (1), (2), (3), (4) or (5)` AND `the person is an officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, as section 408(3) gives that meaning`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question; split site (i)): "and every officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, shall each be guilty of an offence"

-- src:26384 | (6) If a company or foreign company fails to comply with
-- src:26385 | subsection (1), (2), (3), (4) or (5), the company or foreign
-- src:26386 | company, and every officer of the company or foreign company
-- src:26387 | who is in default, shall each be guilty of an offence and shall each be
-- src:26388 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $25,000.
@ref s 386AKA(6) (src:26384-26388)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company fails to comply with subsection (1), (2), (3), (4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company or foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, as section 408(3) gives that meaning` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 386AKA(6) the most the company or foreign company or an officer in default may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF (IF `the person is the company or foreign company`
        THEN `s 386AKA(6) the company or foreign company is guilty of the offence` `the company or foreign company fails to comply with subsection (1), (2), (3), (4) or (5)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        ELSE `s 386AKA(6) the officer of the company or foreign company is guilty of the offence` `the company or foreign company fails to comply with subsection (1), (2), (3), (4) or (5)` `the person is an officer of the company or foreign company who is in default, as section 408(3) gives that meaning` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

§ `Section 386AL: nominee directors`

-- "31 March 2017" (s 386AL(1), (2)).
`s 386AL(1) the day 31 March 2017` MEANS Date 31 3 2017

-- (1): a company incorporated on or after 31 March 2017 but before the appointed day.
-- src:26394 | 386AL.—(1) A director of a company incorporated on or after
-- src:26395 | 31 March 2017 but before the appointed day —
-- src:26397 | (a) who is a nominee on the date of incorporation must inform
-- src:26398 | the company of that fact and provide such prescribed
-- src:26399 | particulars of the person for whom the director is a
-- src:26400 | nominee within 30 days after the date of incorporation; or
-- src:26404 | (b) who becomes a nominee after the date of incorporation
-- src:26405 | must inform the company of that fact and provide such
-- src:26406 | prescribed particulars of the person for whom the director
-- src:26407 | is a nominee within 30 days after the director becomes a
-- src:26408 | nominee.
@ref s 386AL(1) (src:26394-26408)
GIVEN `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
      `the appointed day under section 386AL(9)` IS A DATE
      `the director was a nominee on the date of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director becomes a nominee after the date of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the director becomes a nominee` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 386AL(1) the last day by which the director must have informed the company` MEANS
    IF    `the date the company was incorporated` AT LEAST `s 386AL(1) the day 31 March 2017`
       AND `the date the company was incorporated` LESS THAN `the appointed day under section 386AL(9)`
    THEN (IF `the director was a nominee on the date of incorporation`
          THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date the company was incorporated` 30 Days)
          ELSE (IF `the director becomes a nominee after the date of incorporation` AND `the date the director becomes a nominee` GREATER THAN `the date the company was incorporated`
                THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date the director becomes a nominee` 30 Days)
                ELSE NOTHING))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraphs (a) and (b) speak of a director "who is a nominee on the date of incorporation" and one "who becomes a nominee after the date of incorporation"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1) speaks of "A director of a company incorporated on or after 31 March 2017 but before the appointed day"

-- (1A): a company incorporated on or after the appointed day.
-- src:26417 | (1A) A director of a company incorporated on or after the appointed
-- src:26418 | day —
-- src:26420 | (a) who is a nominee on the date of incorporation must inform
-- src:26421 | the company of that fact and provide prescribed particulars
-- src:26422 | of the person for whom the director is a nominee on that
-- src:26423 | date; or
-- src:26425 | (b) who becomes a nominee after the date of incorporation
-- src:26426 | must inform the company of that fact and provide
-- src:26427 | prescribed particulars of the person for whom the
-- src:26428 | director is a nominee within 30 days after the director
-- src:26429 | becomes a nominee.
@ref s 386AL(1A) (src:26417-26429)
GIVEN `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
      `the appointed day under section 386AL(9)` IS A DATE
      `the director was a nominee on the date of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director becomes a nominee after the date of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the director becomes a nominee` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 386AL(1A) the last day by which the director must have informed the company` MEANS
    IF `the date the company was incorporated` AT LEAST `the appointed day under section 386AL(9)`
    THEN (IF `the director was a nominee on the date of incorporation`
          THEN JUST `the date the company was incorporated`   -- paragraph (a): the director must inform the company and provide the particulars "on that date"
          ELSE (IF `the director becomes a nominee after the date of incorporation` AND `the date the director becomes a nominee` GREATER THAN `the date the company was incorporated`
                THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date the director becomes a nominee` 30 Days)
                ELSE NOTHING))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraphs (a) and (b)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (1A) speaks of "A director of a company incorporated on or after the appointed day"

-- (2): a company incorporated before 31 March 2017. Paragraph (a) is deleted; only a director who becomes a nominee after 31 March 2017 is covered.
-- src:26433 | (2) A director of a company incorporated before 31 March 2017 —
-- src:26435 | (a) [Deleted by Act 23 of 2024 wef 16/06/2025]
-- src:26437 | (b) who becomes a nominee after 31 March 2017 must inform
-- src:26438 | the company of that fact and provide such prescribed
-- src:26439 | particulars of the person for whom the director is a
-- src:26440 | nominee within 30 days after the director becomes a
-- src:26441 | nominee.
@ref s 386AL(2) (src:26433-26441)
GIVEN `the date the company was incorporated` IS A DATE
      `the director becomes a nominee after 31 March 2017` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the director becomes a nominee` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 386AL(2) the last day by which the director must have informed the company` MEANS
    IF `the date the company was incorporated` LESS THAN `s 386AL(1) the day 31 March 2017`
    THEN (IF `the director becomes a nominee after 31 March 2017` AND `the date the director becomes a nominee` GREATER THAN `s 386AL(1) the day 31 March 2017`
          THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date the director becomes a nominee` 30 Days)
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) speaks of a director "who becomes a nominee after 31 March 2017"; paragraph (a) is "[Deleted by Act 23 of 2024 wef 16/06/2025]", so the text states nothing for a director who became a nominee earlier
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) speaks of "A director of a company incorporated before 31 March 2017"

-- (3): any company, whenever incorporated: cessation, and change to the particulars, each within 30 days after.
-- src:26447 | (3) A director of a company (whether incorporated before, on or
-- src:26448 | after the appointed day) must inform the company —
-- src:26450 | (a) that he or she ceases to be a nominee within 30 days after
-- src:26451 | the cessation; and
-- src:26453 | (b) of any change to the particulars provided to the company
-- src:26454 | under this section (whether as in force on or before the
-- src:26455 | appointed day) within 30 days after the change.
@ref s 386AL(3) (src:26447-26455)
GIVEN `the date the director ceased to be a nominee, or the date the particulars provided to the company changed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 386AL(3) the last day by which the director must have informed the company` MEANS
    JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date the director ceased to be a nominee, or the date the particulars provided to the company changed` 30 Days)

-- (4): a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11 on or after the appointed day.
-- src:26459 | (4) A director of a foreign company registered under Division 2 of
-- src:26460 | Part 11 on or after the appointed day —
-- src:26462 | (a) who is a nominee on the date of registration must inform
-- src:26463 | the foreign company of that fact and provide prescribed
-- src:26464 | particulars of the person for whom the director is a
-- src:26465 | nominee on that date; or
-- src:26470 | (b) who becomes a nominee after the date of registration must
-- src:26471 | inform the foreign company of that fact and provide
-- src:26472 | prescribed particulars of the person for whom the director
-- src:26473 | is a nominee within 30 days after the director becomes a
-- src:26474 | nominee.
@ref s 386AL(4) (src:26459-26474)
GIVEN `the date the foreign company was registered` IS A DATE
      `the appointed day under section 386AL(9)` IS A DATE
      `the director was a nominee on the date of registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director becomes a nominee after the date of registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the director becomes a nominee` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 386AL(4) the last day by which the director must have informed the foreign company` MEANS
    IF `the date the foreign company was registered` AT LEAST `the appointed day under section 386AL(9)`
    THEN (IF `the director was a nominee on the date of registration`
          THEN JUST `the date the foreign company was registered`   -- paragraph (a): the director must inform the foreign company and provide the particulars "on that date"
          ELSE (IF `the director becomes a nominee after the date of registration` AND `the date the director becomes a nominee` GREATER THAN `the date the foreign company was registered`
                THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date the director becomes a nominee` 30 Days)
                ELSE NOTHING))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraphs (a) and (b)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (4) speaks of "A director of a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11 on or after the appointed day"

-- (5): a foreign company registered before the appointed day.
-- src:26478 | (5) A director of a foreign company registered under Division 2 of
-- src:26479 | Part 11 before the appointed day —
-- src:26481 | (a) who is a nominee on the appointed day must inform the
-- src:26482 | foreign company of that fact and provide prescribed
-- src:26483 | particulars of the person for whom the director is a
-- src:26484 | nominee within 60 days after that day; or
-- src:26486 | (b) who becomes a nominee after the appointed day must
-- src:26487 | inform the foreign company of that fact and provide
-- src:26488 | prescribed particulars of the person for whom the director
-- src:26489 | is a nominee within 30 days after the director becomes a
-- src:26490 | nominee.
@ref s 386AL(5) (src:26478-26490)
GIVEN `the date the foreign company was registered` IS A DATE
      `the appointed day under section 386AL(9)` IS A DATE
      `the director was a nominee on the appointed day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director becomes a nominee after the appointed day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the director becomes a nominee` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 386AL(5) the last day by which the director must have informed the foreign company` MEANS
    IF `the date the foreign company was registered` LESS THAN `the appointed day under section 386AL(9)`
    THEN (IF `the director was a nominee on the appointed day`
          THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the appointed day under section 386AL(9)` 60 Days)
          ELSE (IF `the director becomes a nominee after the appointed day` AND `the date the director becomes a nominee` GREATER THAN `the appointed day under section 386AL(9)`
                THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date the director becomes a nominee` 30 Days)
                ELSE NOTHING))   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraphs (a) and (b)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (5) speaks of "A director of a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11 before the appointed day"

-- (5A): a foreign company mentioned in (4) or (5): cessation and change, each within 30 days after.
-- src:26494 | (5A) A director of a foreign company mentioned in subsection (4)
-- src:26495 | or (5) must inform the foreign company —
-- src:26497 | (a) that he or she ceases to be a nominee within 30 days after
-- src:26498 | the cessation; and
-- src:26500 | (b) of any change to the particulars provided to the foreign
-- src:26501 | company under that subsection within 30 days after the
-- src:26502 | change.
@ref s 386AL(5A) (src:26494-26502)
GIVEN `the foreign company is registered under Division 2 of Part 11` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the director ceased to be a nominee, or the date the particulars provided to the foreign company changed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 386AL(5A) the last day by which the director must have informed the foreign company` MEANS
    IF `the foreign company is registered under Division 2 of Part 11`
    THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date the director ceased to be a nominee, or the date the particulars provided to the foreign company changed` 30 Days)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (5A) speaks of "A director of a foreign company mentioned in subsection (4) or (5)"

-- The company or foreign company, and the day to count from, together.
DECLARE `s 386AL kind of body` IS ONE OF
    `s 386AL a company`
    `s 386AL a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11`

GIVEN kind IS A `s 386AL kind of body`
      `the date the company was incorporated or the foreign company was registered` IS A DATE
      `the appointed day under section 386AL(9)` IS A DATE
      `the director was a nominee on the date of incorporation or registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director was a nominee on the appointed day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director becomes a nominee after that date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the director becomes a nominee` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 386AL(1), (1A), (2), (4) and (5) the last day by which the director must have informed the company or foreign company` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 386AL a company` THEN
        CONSIDER `s 386AL(1) the last day by which the director must have informed the company` `the date the company was incorporated or the foreign company was registered` `the appointed day under section 386AL(9)` `the director was a nominee on the date of incorporation or registration` `the director becomes a nominee after that date` `the date the director becomes a nominee`
        WHEN JUST d THEN JUST d
        WHEN NOTHING THEN
            CONSIDER `s 386AL(1A) the last day by which the director must have informed the company` `the date the company was incorporated or the foreign company was registered` `the appointed day under section 386AL(9)` `the director was a nominee on the date of incorporation or registration` `the director becomes a nominee after that date` `the date the director becomes a nominee`
            WHEN JUST d THEN JUST d
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 386AL(2) the last day by which the director must have informed the company` `the date the company was incorporated or the foreign company was registered` `the director becomes a nominee after that date` `the date the director becomes a nominee`
    WHEN `s 386AL a foreign company registered under Division 2 of Part 11` THEN
        CONSIDER `s 386AL(4) the last day by which the director must have informed the foreign company` `the date the company was incorporated or the foreign company was registered` `the appointed day under section 386AL(9)` `the director was a nominee on the date of incorporation or registration` `the director becomes a nominee after that date` `the date the director becomes a nominee`
        WHEN JUST d THEN JUST d
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 386AL(5) the last day by which the director must have informed the foreign company` `the date the company was incorporated or the foreign company was registered` `the appointed day under section 386AL(9)` `the director was a nominee on the appointed day` `the director becomes a nominee after that date` `the date the director becomes a nominee`

-- (6): the offence of the director.
-- src:26506 | (6) If a director fails to comply with subsection (1), (1A), (2), (3),
-- src:26507 | (4), (5) or (5A), the director shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:26508 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $25,000.
@ref s 386AL(6) (src:26506-26508)
GIVEN `the director fails to comply with subsection (1), (1A), (2), (3), (4), (5) or (5A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AL(6) the director is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the director fails to comply with subsection (1), (1A), (2), (3), (4), (5) or (5A)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the provision's own question; split site (i)): "If a director fails to comply with subsection (1), (1A), (2), (3), (4), (5) or (5A), the director shall be guilty of an offence"

-- src:26506 | (6) If a director fails to comply with subsection (1), (1A), (2), (3),
-- src:26507 | (4), (5) or (5A), the director shall be guilty of an offence and shall be
-- src:26508 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $25,000.
@ref s 386AL(6) (src:26506-26508)
GIVEN `the director fails to comply with subsection (1), (1A), (2), (3), (4), (5) or (5A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 386AL(6) the most the director may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 386AL(6) the director is guilty of the offence` `the director fails to comply with subsection (1), (1A), (2), (3), (4), (5) or (5A)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 25000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

-- (8): a director is a nominee ("is a nominee if": a failed "if", marginal reading (a)).
-- src:26514 | (8) In this section and section 386AKA, a director is a nominee if
-- src:26515 | the director is accustomed or under an obligation whether formal or
-- src:26520 | informal to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or
-- src:26521 | wishes of any other person.
@ref s 386AL(8) (src:26514-26521)
GIVEN `the director is accustomed or under an obligation, whether formal or informal, to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 386AL(8) the director is a nominee` MEANS
    IF `the director is accustomed or under an obligation, whether formal or informal, to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of any other person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", marginal reading (a)): "a director is a nominee if the director is accustomed or under an obligation whether formal or informal to act in accordance with the directions, instructions or wishes of any other person"

-- (9): the appointed day is supplied: the date section 8 of the 2024 Act commenced.
-- src:26527 | (9) In this section, “appointed day” means the date of
-- src:26528 | commencement of section 8 of the Companies and Limited
-- src:26529 | Liability Partnerships (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2024.
@ref s 386AL(9) (src:26527-26529)
GIVEN `the date section 8 of the Companies and Limited Liability Partnerships (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2024 commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 386AL(9) "appointed day" the appointed day` MEANS `the date section 8 of the Companies and Limited Liability Partnerships (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2024 commenced`

-- The duties, one for each paragraph that gives a time. The party is the director; the prescribed particulars are an input of the notification itself.
-- src:26397 | (a) who is a nominee on the date of incorporation must inform
-- src:26398 | the company of that fact and provide such prescribed
-- src:26399 | particulars of the person for whom the director is a
-- src:26400 | nominee within 30 days after the date of incorporation; or
@ref s 386AL(1)(a) (src:26397-26400)
GIVEN `the director` IS A Party
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 386AL act`
`s 386AL(1)(a) a director of a company incorporated on or after 31 March 2017 but before the appointed day who is a nominee on the date of incorporation must inform the company within 30 days after the date of incorporation` MEANS
    PARTY `the director`
    MUST `s 386AL(1)(a) inform the company that the director is a nominee and provide the prescribed particulars of the person for whom the director is a nominee`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the director` BECAUSE "the director did not inform the company that the director is a nominee, and provide the prescribed particulars, within 30 days after the date of incorporation (s 386AL(1)(a), (6))"
